00:43:00.350 --> 00:43:01.090
What's up, dude?

00:43:11.660 --> 00:43:12.100
What's up?

00:45:01.400 --> 00:45:01.700
We'll be right back.

00:45:33.100 --> 00:45:34.180
Get ready to move a little closer.

00:45:35.820 --> 00:45:36.340
We'll see.

00:45:45.750 --> 00:45:46.850
It looks like a monkey.

00:45:47.320 --> 00:45:47.580
Monkey.

00:46:00.350 --> 00:46:03.350
Hey, tell her her voice is like a tinkling piano.

00:46:03.610 --> 00:46:05.630
And that she's as funny as a rubber chicken.

00:46:05.950 --> 00:46:08.610
And her eyes are like two computer screens.

00:46:09.010 --> 00:46:12.410
Huh? Your eyes are like chickens,

00:46:12.490 --> 00:46:14.490
and your voice is a tinkling computer.

00:46:16.670 --> 00:46:19.280
Tell her there comes one moment.

00:46:19.600 --> 00:46:21.300
There comes one moment.

00:46:21.560 --> 00:46:22.580
When Beauty stands.

00:46:23.020 --> 00:46:24.800
When Beauty, stand by.

00:46:26.470 --> 00:46:28.650
Three, proceed to the corner of Fifth and Main.

00:46:43.210 --> 00:46:44.860
You like her shoes.

00:46:45.040 --> 00:46:46.240
Tell her you like her nose.

00:46:47.810 --> 00:46:49.440
Tell her she's cool.

00:46:49.830 --> 00:46:50.650
Tell her she's...

00:46:51.230 --> 00:46:55.790
She smells good.

00:46:55.930 --> 00:46:57.210
Tell her she's won the lottery.

00:47:33.070 --> 00:47:34.390
Why, thank you, Gonzo.

00:48:00.190 --> 00:48:13.070
It's a good idea to look closely before you decide if you like something or not.

00:48:13.230 --> 00:48:14.710
That's a good idea, Mary.

00:48:14.990 --> 00:48:16.530
Yeah, that's a very good idea.

00:48:44.040 --> 00:48:45.150
What do you say, genius?
